## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to design a runtime-extendable, observable notification system using plug‑in sinks and safe parallel dispatch.

## Key Concepts

- Runtime registries
- Plugin/Strategy patterns
- Concurrency and backoff
- Idempotency and deduplication
- Observability (metrics, traces)

## Code Example

```javascript
interface Sink { send(message: string, id: string): Promise<void> }
type SinkFactory = () => Sink

class SinkRegistry {
  private map = new Map<string, SinkFactory>()
  register(name: string, factory: SinkFactory) { this.map.set(name, factory) }
  create(name: string): Sink | null { const f = this.map.get(name); return f ? f() : null }
}

class NotificationRouter {
  constructor(private registry: SinkRegistry) {}
  async route(routeId: string, message: string, id: string, sinkNames: string[]) {
    const sinks = sinkNames.map(n => this.registry.create(n)).filter(Boolean) as Sink[]
    await Promise.all(sinks.map(s => s.send(message, id)))
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test idempotency and duplicate suppression?
- How would you handle sink-specific failures without blocking others?
- How would you instrument with metrics and tracing?

## Why This Is Asked
Explores dynamic extensibility and runtime hot-swapping of behavior without redeployments, crucial for scalable data platforms.

## Key Concepts
- Plugin registry mapping (type, version) to handlers
- Versioned command schemas and graceful deprecation
- Isolation via worker pools or process boundaries

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal interface sketch (TypeScript-like)
interface Command {
  execute(ctx: any, payload: any): Promise<void>;
}
interface PluginFactory {
  create(payload: any): Command;
}
class Registry {
  private map = new Map<string, Map<number, PluginFactory>>();

  register(type: string, version: number, factory: PluginFactory) {
    if (!this.map.has(type)) {
      this.map.set(type, new Map());
    }
    this.map.get(type)!.set(version, factory);
  }

  create(type: string, version: number, payload: any): Command | null {
    return this.map.get(type)?.get(version)?.create(payload) || null;
  }
}
```

